{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8750","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"704, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"704","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8750","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"Ranchos Church","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Ranchos Church","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Ranchos Church, 1930. Oil on canvas, 24 x 36 inches. Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met). Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1961. © Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1961","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Infor. from Miss Bry at An Amer. Place, July 1949. . . . On permanent loan to the Metropolitan Museum of Art from Georgia O'Keeffe as part of the Alfred Stieglitz Coll.\" Whitney Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks indicate that this painting was included in the 1931 New York (An American Place) exhibition, whose checklist includes three works titled \"Ranchos Church, New Mexico.\" This work is not among the three paintings of churches pictured in the 1931 New York (An American Place) Stieglitz installation photographs, see cat. nos. 660, 703, 705 and Appendix III, figures 42, 47, 48. See cat. no. 705, a painting exhibited in 1931 and, again, in 1931–32 after being reworked in the area of the sky. Titled *Ranchos de Taos Church – 31 – N.M.* by O'Keeffe on Abiquiú Notebooks photograph. See also cat. nos. 1843, 1845, 1871, 1872. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 24 x 36 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"A tan-colored adobe church, seen from the side, stands on uneven ground in a similar shade of light brown. Behind the structure is a textured, clouded sky.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"24 x 36 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"selected_references","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/selected_references"}],"content":"Ray Bethers. How Paintings Happen. New York, 1951, p. 119, ill. \n \nGeorge Heard Hamilton. \"The Alfred Stieglitz Collection.\" Metropolitan Museum Journal 3 (1970), p. 392. \n \nCharles Child Eldredge. \"Georgia O'Keeffe: The Development of an American Modern.\" PhD diss., University of Minnesota, 1971, p. 66. \n \nGeorgia O'Keeffe. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1976, text facing pl. 63, ill. \n \nPaul Goldberger. \"Art: Architectural View by American Painters.\" New York Times (October 30, 1980), p. C22. \n \nTheodore Wolff. \"Art that Walks a Tightrope.\" Christian Science Monitor (November 24, 1980), p. 18. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. \"Georgia O'Keeffe.\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 42 (Fall 1984), pp. 38, 40–41, 60, ill. \n \nD. H. Lawrence. \"Rings um mich her, die grosse, ungebrochene Weite.\" DU (May 1987), p. 6, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1988, pp. 63, 65–67, ill. \n \nAnita Pollitzer. A Woman on Paper: Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1988, p. 206, ill. \n \nDoris Bry in Georgia O'Keeffe, in the West. Ed. Doris Bry and Nicholas Callaway. New York, 1989, pl. 5. \n \nSarah Whitaker Peters. Becoming O'Keeffe: The Early Years. New York, 1991, pp. 196, 348. \n \nCharles Child Eldredge. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1991, pp. 105–6, ill. \n \nMaria Costantino. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1994, pp. 116–17, ill. \n \nJula Dech. Georgia O'Keeffe: Gemälde. Munich, 1995, pl. 24. \n \nRobert Hughes. American Visions: The Epic History of Art in America. New York, 1997, pp. 12–13, fig. 7. \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes. Georgia O'Keeffe: Catalogue Raisonné. New Haven, Conn., 1999, vol. 1, pp. 422–23, no. 704, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. London, 2001, pp. 110–11, fig. 72. \n \nJohn Carlin and Jonathan Fineberg. Imagining America: Icons of 20th-Century American Art. New Haven and London, 2005, p. 46, ill. \n \nKatja Fauth. Modernist Visions in Taos: Mabel Dodge Luhan and the Artists of the Stieglitz Circle. Marburg, Germany, 2009, pp. 158, 181, fig. 23. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger in Stieglitz and His Artists: Matisse to O'Keeffe. The Alfred Stieglitz Collection in The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Ed. Lisa Mintz Messinger. Exh. cat., The Metropolitan Museum of Art. New York, 2011, pp. 14, 193, 201, 280, no. 187, ill. (color). \n \nSarah Greenough, ed. My Faraway One: Selected Letters of Georgia O'Keeffe and Alfred Stieglitz. Vol. 1, 1915–1933. New Haven, Conn., 2011, pp. 540–41. \n \nLauren Kroiz in Katherine M. Bourguignon Lauren Kroiz and Leo G. Mazow. America's Cool Modernism: O'Keeffe to Hopper. Exh. cat., Ashmolean Museum. Oxford, England, 2018, p. 65, no. 56, ill. p. 151 (color).","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Ranchos Church, 1930","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"The artist (1930–61; on extended loan to MMA, 1949–61; her gift as part of the Alfred Stieglitz Collection to MMA) (Source: The Met, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/884934/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digita